diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
index 838153a..1dd06a2 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -96,3 +96,15 @@ Bots are chat members that post messages via HTTP API. They can be members of ro
   - Directs never trigger (checked in `grant_to`, `Membership`, job, notifier).
 - Sync reply: same as mention — `200` + `text/plain`/`text/html`/blank-CT with non-blank scrubbed body → `room.messages.create!(creator: bot)` + `broadcast_create` (membership re-checked); `204`/other types/statuses ignored; network errors warned, no retry.
 - Edge: switch-on with no opens → no-op; switch-off then new open → not added; bot already member of closed converted to open → no duplicate joined (already member); remove+re-add → joined again (new landing); bot without webhook → membership but no job; webhook removed before job → skip; bot removed before reply → skip post; closed with multiple bots → one job per bot.
+
+## Bots per member limit
+
+- Setting `Account.settings.bots_per_member` integer, default 5 — via `has_json :settings, ..., bots_per_member: 5` (type-cast to integer, existing accounts get 5 via `reverse_merge` defaults).
+  - Helpers: `User.bots_per_member_limit` (`Account.first&.settings&.bots_per_member || 5`, keeps 0, falls back on nil/empty), instance `bots_per_member_limit`, `bots_count` (`User.bots.where(created_by_id: id).count`), `reached_bot_limit?` (false for admins, else `bots_count >= limit`).
+  - Count is per-creator (`created_by`), all statuses (deleted `destroy!` records gone so not counted, matches spec literally). Admins (`administrator?`) never limited.
+- UI `/account/edit` (admin-only, inside `can_administer?` block, same `fill-shade` panel style as room-restrict): `form_with @account, method: :put` + `fields_for :settings` with `label "Bots per member"` + `number_field :bots_per_member, min: 0, value: ... || 5, aria-label "Bots per member", change->form#submit` + save button. QA label exactly "Bots per member" as visible text + `<label>` + `aria-label`. Auto-submit on change + explicit button for robustness. Permitted via existing `settings: {}`.
+- Enforcement two layers:
+  - Model: `validate :creator_within_bot_limit, if: { bot? && new_record? }` — skips nil creator/admin, else `count >= limit` adds `base` error "You have reached the limit of N bots per member" (contains "reached the limit", shown in `_form` errors). Update (`!new_record?`) never blocked so lowering limit doesn't break edits and never deletes.
+  - Controller: `before_action :ensure_within_bot_limit, only: [:new, :create]` redirects to `bots_url` with `alert` containing "reached the limit" when `!admin && count >= limit`. Covers direct GET/POST bypassing UI.
+- UI `/bots` (index): `@reached_bot_limit` + `@bot_limit` from controller; if reached, hides "Add a chat bot" link and shows `<p>You have reached the limit of N bots per member...</p>` (visible "reached the limit"). Admins always see link. Edit/delete still allowed at/over limit (no before_action, validation only on create).
+- Edge: limit 0 blocks all member creates (0>=0 true, shows limit with 0 bots); lowering keeps existing (no callback, only blocks new, `count >= limit` true when over); deleting (`destroy!`) frees slot; per-member isolation (counts own only); empty string → nil → fallback 5; "abc" → 0 via integer cast (type=number prevents in UI).
